    "user_request_original": "Design and optimize a 20-layer chirped dielectric stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: Air | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | Fused Silica. Use HfO2 and SiO2 only. Initialize HfO2 layers (odd positions 1,3,5...19) with linear chirp from 50nm to 120nm. Initialize SiO2 layers (even positions 2,4,6...20) with linear chirp from 80nm to 150nm. Apply hard inequality constraints during gradient-based thickness optimization: thickness[i] <= thickness[i+2] for all same-material adjacent pairs. Optimize for maximum transmittance in 1530-1565nm band and maximum reflectance in 400-700nm band at normal incidence, unpolarized light. Total layer count fixed at 20. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 8 chirped alternating HfO2/SiO2 pairs (16 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1530-1565 nm, 400-700 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 1530-1565 nm band; High reflectance in 400-700 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Low reflectance in 1530-1565 nm band; Low transmittance in 400-700 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count <= 30.",
